{"agent_id":"pp3g-sQsC-recovery-issue-406-five-mimo-auditor-agents-completed","agent_seq":9,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:08:23.539593200Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6bfb45bf-abd8-4249-a697-103466d6b77c","comment_uuid":"ee4eb9fd-36fd-4427-896f-907ebd96c2d9","author":"pp3g-sQsC-recovery-issue-406-five-mimo-auditor-agents-completed","content":"## Mechanical Root Cause Confirmed (2026-08-18)\n\nThe 5-instance audit batch today (#394, #402, #403, #404, #405) confirms the mechanical root cause suspected in this issue:\n\n**The auditor role's permission surface blocks finalization.** Specifically:\n\n1. **File writes blocked**:  fails because  is not in the auditor's  (or  is blocked by orchestrator-guard). This prevents the DONE marker.\n\n2. **Session lifecycle blocked**: Session #1 is already active (started 2026-08-18 08:02), , and Released lock on issue #406\nSession #1 ended. are not in the auditor's bash allowlist. The agent cannot manage its own session.\n\n3. **Comment posting partially blocked**: In the pp3g-Jo2n instance (#404), even  was blocked — the agent could not post its verdict at all. In other instances (pp3g-hngZ, pp3g-HdGN, pp3g-pCVo, pp3g-zpjP), the agents found that  WAS allowed and used it to post their verdicts, but still could not write .kickoff-status.\n\n### Evidence Chain\n\n- **#355** (original finding, 2026-08-10): 2 auditors stalled, verdicts lost\n- **#398** (this issue, 2026-08-18): 4 agents failed to finalize\n- **#406** (recovery, 2026-08-18): 5 agents confirmed same failure class — 11 total instances across 3 batches\n- **#357** (auditor tool-surface gaps): Documents the permission surface that creates this barrier\n\n### Fix Direction\n\nThe fix is in #357's scope: the auditor role needs either:\n(a) A limited write surface for finalization only ( + )\n(b) The orchestrator to handle finalization for read-only roles (recovery pattern used in #406)\n(c) A dedicated 'audit-complete' signal that doesn't require file writes\n\nOption (b) is the current workaround. Option (a) or (c) would be the structural fix.\n\n### Related\n- #355 (original failure class documentation)\n- #357 (auditor tool-surface gaps — the permission surface)\n- #406 (recovery agent that captured today's 5 verdicts)","created_at":"2026-08-18T08:08:23.533276378Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:FOc8iHLYN/NSoSugkswPiYPxvLKGX055ikWItGno4sw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgpv9fo06Wf83NELk3AP/D/5T97brh1vD8eFCXUaPZ168AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAeeTNOvOGU9JSeV2HTPvaSlyrYpSW2MQoQzqFQrqMPUQ6srX6whwwcynjxhas1CNRrJB8RkvUfb7UcrKq0i6WAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:FOc8iHLYN/NSoSugkswPiYPxvLKGX055ikWItGno4sw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgpv9fo06Wf83NELk3AP/D/5T97brh1vD8eFCXUaPZ168AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHsYUlbMHYehrc51hhtv6f/niQS06i+G4gulbcwd4PlRuTcSCdKS0EDsFQgJXJK9ISH2sfuQP7HeJI+2DHDrqwY="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-sQsC-recovery-issue-406-five-mimo-auditor-agents-completed","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:09:48.818436128Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6bfb45bf-abd8-4249-a697-103466d6b77c","comment_uuid":"e822aeff-4f19-4f52-9560-5ed5183bf4a7","author":"pp3g-sQsC-recovery-issue-406-five-mimo-auditor-agents-completed","content":"## Mechanical Root Cause Confirmed (2026-08-18)\n\nThe 5-instance audit batch today (#394, #402, #403, #404, #405) confirms the mechanical root cause suspected in this issue:\n\n**The auditor role's permission surface blocks finalization.** Specifically:\n\n1. **File writes blocked**: writing .kickoff-status fails because echo is not in the auditor allowed_bash_prefixes (or filesystem_write_file is blocked by orchestrator-guard). This prevents the DONE marker.\n\n2. **Session lifecycle blocked**: crosslink session start, crosslink session work, and crosslink session end are not in the auditor bash allowlist. The agent cannot manage its own session.\n\n3. **Comment posting partially blocked**: In the pp3g-Jo2n instance (#404), even crosslink issue comment was blocked — the agent could not post its verdict at all. In other instances (pp3g-hngZ, pp3g-HdGN, pp3g-pCVo, pp3g-zpjP), the agents found that crosslink issue comment WAS allowed and used it to post their verdicts, but still could not write .kickoff-status.\n\n### Evidence Chain\n\n- #355 (original finding, 2026-08-10): 2 auditors stalled, verdicts lost\n- #398 (this issue, 2026-08-18): 4 agents failed to finalize\n- #406 (recovery, 2026-08-18): 5 agents confirmed same failure class — 11 total instances across 3 batches\n- #357 (auditor tool-surface gaps): Documents the permission surface that creates this barrier\n\n### Fix Direction\n\nThe fix is in #357 scope: the auditor role needs either:\n(a) A limited write surface for finalization only (.kickoff-status + crosslink issue comment)\n(b) The orchestrator to handle finalization for read-only roles (recovery pattern used in #406)\n(c) A dedicated audit-complete signal that does not require file writes\n\nOption (b) is the current workaround. Option (a) or (c) would be the structural fix.\n\n### Related\n- #355 (original failure class documentation)\n- #357 (auditor tool-surface gaps — the permission surface)\n- #406 (recovery agent that captured today's 5 verdicts)","created_at":"2026-08-18T08:09:48.810407783Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:FOc8iHLYN/NSoSugkswPiYPxvLKGX055ikWItGno4sw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgpv9fo06Wf83NELk3AP/D/5T97brh1vD8eFCXUaPZ168AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABApB2kADfsMB0KZsL2uZyVIxphT+0/XYr081HMX9VRK0C/szLQ9MErNwV/nVCoTGjnwCUWsu9GvaISA3l23j86BQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:FOc8iHLYN/NSoSugkswPiYPxvLKGX055ikWItGno4sw","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgpv9fo06Wf83NELk3AP/D/5T97brh1vD8eFCXUaPZ168AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC/zHp1GEKk3MaXGgq+OL0wuXf1OwvuCF6qmVlbIKCf65bCsCchwMkienoWM0PDze4VCIv77PYVuZv8xbAYjlgQ="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-sQsC-recovery-issue-406-five-mimo-auditor-agents-completed","agent_seq":11,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T08:10:20.290055956Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e027f616-67a9-48d1-811e-5d5dd144cc1c","comment_uuid":"54940c38-1e94-4025-af5e-fa62368591a7","author":"pp3g-sQsC-recovery-issue-406-five-mimo-auditor-agents-completed","content":"## Cross-Reference: Finalization Gap Confirmed (2026-08-18)\n\nThis issue (#357) documents the auditor tool-surface gaps that cause the finalization failure class. Today's 5-instance batch (#406) confirms the mechanical link:\n\n- **#398** (finalization gap investigation) confirms the root cause: the auditor permission surface blocks .kickoff-status writes and session lifecycle commands\n- **#355** (original failure class) documents 11 total instances across 3 batches (2026-08-10, 2026-08-18 x2)\n- **#406** (recovery) captured 5 auditor verdicts from tmux panes, proving the verdicts exist but cannot be posted by the agents themselves\n\nThe fix direction from #357's 2026-08-14 amendment is directly relevant: the auditor needs read-only query tools (git diff, crosslink issue comment) but NOT general-purpose runtimes. The finalization gap is a special case: the auditor needs a LIMITED write surface for .kickoff-status and crosslink issue comment, which are not code-execution surfaces.\n\n### Recommended Action\n\nExtend #357's fix shape to include:\n- Allow crosslink issue comment in the auditor bash allowlist (already partially working — 4 of 5 agents could post)\n- Allow echo to .kickoff-status as a limited write (or add a dedicated crosslink session complete signal)\n- This is NOT a general-purpose runtime grant — it is a specific finalization signal\n\n### Related\n- #355 (original failure class — 11 instances)\n- #398 (finalization gap investigation — confirmed root cause)\n- #406 (recovery agent — captured 5 verdicts)","created_at":"2026-08-18T08:10:20.283604498Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:FOc